Chapter: TreeCheck
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Safari chapter Camera
  cites Safari chapter Paint
  cites Safari chapter Tree
  cites Judge chapter Grade
  cites Gold chapter TreeGold

 Grade the Tree and Paint ports against wasm/tree.zig driving wasm/paint.zig.

 Seam 3 on one object. The oracle does not read return values -- tree.draw writes
 into paint's real buffer -- so the gold is the words the game actually put on the
 wire, decoded back into four streams. Tags, colours and point counts compare
 EXACTLY; strengths and coordinates carry the width tolerance.

 That split matters. A wrong tag or a wrong point count is a structural error and
 no tolerance should ever hide one; a coordinate differing in the seventh digit is
 the f32/f64 width and nothing else.

 COORDINATES TAKE THE MIXED PIXEL GATE, and that is not a loosening. A screen
 y is computed as 300 minus a term of about the same size, so a y near the horizon
 is a small DIFFERENCE OF TWO LARGE NUMBERS and cancellation amplifies f32's
 relative error by the ratio between them. Measured on this frame's first cone
 tier: y = 20.6068 carries a relative gap of 1.3e-6, about fifteen times f32
 epsilon, exactly the 300/20.6 the cancellation predicts. A purely relative gate would have to
 be loosened everywhere to admit that. A purely absolute one breaks the other way on
 coordinates flung far off screen by the near plane. The floor plus a relative term
 covers both, and on this canvas it is about a thousandth of a pixel.

 THE CASES ARE BRANCHES, NOT COVERAGE: a far tree (flat triangles, bar trunk), a
 mid tree (cone hulls), a near tree (cone hulls and a round-shaded trunk), a tree
 close enough that its widest tiers cross MIN_CONE_FORWARD and bail from cone back
 to triangle -- one tree emitting both crown forms -- and a tree too small to draw,
 which must emit nothing at all.

 We say:

Section: The Cases

  case-far : List DrawCmd
  case-far = tree-draw (0.0 - 9.0) 140.0 7.0 3108154 focal camera-w False False 0.0

  case-mid : List DrawCmd
  case-mid = tree-draw 12.0 46.0 8.5 3108154 focal camera-w False True 0.45

  case-near : List DrawCmd
  case-near = tree-draw (0.0 - 5.5) 11.0 6.25 3504447 focal camera-w True True 1.0

  case-close : List DrawCmd
  case-close = tree-draw 1.5 2.0 9.0 3108154 focal camera-w True True 1.0

  case-tiny : List DrawCmd
  case-tiny = tree-draw 40.0 4000.0 6.0 3108154 focal camera-w False False 0.0

  all-cmds : List DrawCmd
  all-cmds = case-far & case-mid & case-near & case-close & case-tiny

Section: Streams

 The same four streams the probe decoded out of the buffer, in the same order.

  cmd-tags : List DrawCmd, Integer -> List Integer
  cmd-tags (cs) (i) =
    if i >= list-length cs then []
    else [(list-at cs i).tag] & cmd-tags cs (i + 1)

  cmd-colors : List DrawCmd, Integer -> List Integer
  cmd-colors (cs) (i) =
    if i >= list-length cs then []
    else [(list-at cs i).color] & cmd-colors cs (i + 1)

  cmd-counts : List DrawCmd, Integer -> List Integer
  cmd-counts (cs) (i) =
    if i >= list-length cs then []
    else [list-length (list-at cs i).pts / 2] & cmd-counts cs (i + 1)

  cmd-strengths : List DrawCmd, Integer -> List Real
  cmd-strengths (cs) (i) =
    if i >= list-length cs then []
    else [(list-at cs i).strength] & cmd-strengths cs (i + 1)

  cmd-coords : List DrawCmd, Integer -> List Real
  cmd-coords (cs) (i) =
    if i >= list-length cs then []
    else (list-at cs i).pts & cmd-coords cs (i + 1)

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (grade-ints "tree-tags     " (cmd-tags all-cmds 0) g-tree-tags)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints "tree-colors   " (cmd-colors all-cmds 0) g-tree-colors)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints "tree-counts   " (cmd-counts all-cmds 0) g-tree-counts)
    print-line-uni (grade-rel  "tree-strengths" (cmd-strengths all-cmds 0) g-tree-strengths 0.000001)
    print-line-uni (grade-px "tree-coords   " (cmd-coords all-cmds 0) g-tree-coords 0.001 0.000001)
  end
